  "narration": {
    "voice": "en-US-AvaNeural",
    "alignment": "Whisper tiny.en word timestamps measured against final narration waveform",
    "phrases": [
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "At Kurukshetra, the archer Arjuna looked across the armies and saw his own teachers, cousins and relatives facing him.",
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 9.38
      },
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "Victory suddenly looked like a catastrophe.",
        "start": 9.8,
        "end": 11.98
      },
      {
        "scene": "S02",
        "text": "His bow lowered.",
        "start": 12.98,
        "end": 13.92
      },
      {
        "scene": "S02",
        "text": "He asked what meaning a kingdom could have if obtaining it required killing those he loved and respected.",
        "start": 14.62,
        "end": 20.74
      },
      {
        "scene": "S03",
        "text": "His charioteer Krishna answered with a long teaching on duty, action, the self and the difficulty of living rightly amid conflict.",
        "start": 21.9,
        "end": 31.26
      },
      {
        "scene": "S04",
        "text": "The teaching did not make the battlefield disappear.",
        "start": 32.42,
        "end": 35.42
      },
      {
        "scene": "S04",
        "text": "It challenged Arjuna to confront his obligations without pretending he could avoid consequences.",
        "start": 36.1,
        "end": 41.68
      },
      {
        "scene": "S05",
        "text": "In the Gita, Krishna reveals an overwhelming cosmic form in which creation and destruction are entwined.",
        "start": 43.1,
        "end": 50.88
      },
      {
        "scene": "S05",
        "text": "Arjuna sees a scale far beyond his individual fear.",
        "start": 51.66,
        "end": 55.173
      },
      {
        "scene": "S06",
        "text": "The dialogue ends with Arjuna prepared to act.",
        "start": 56.273,
        "end": 60.12
      },
      {
        "scene": "S06",
        "text": "Whether one agrees with his decision or not, the story refuses to make moral conflict painless.",
        "start": 60.46,
        "end": 67.62
      }
    ],
